  "surprise": "613 (638/623/578) vs 687: discard. Pretraining looked healthy and inside every predicted band: 3304/3318/3334 steps (ratio 0.73, the probe's 0.74), val loss 0.0865/0.0852/0.0808 at or below 153's 0.088, held-out greedy 0.961 on all seeds. The damage is entirely in RL sampling at T 0.8: round-1 targets solved 515/339/593 vs 153's 766/747/694 and round-1 sample acc 0.15/0.09/0.19 vs 0.27, hitting the preregistered falsifier (a seed below 550) on two seeds; expert iteration recovered most of it (round 4: 1111/1079/1078 vs 1157/1168/1191) but never caught up. So bounding the logits to cosine x gains (gains under AdamW 1e-3 move at most ~3 in 3,300 steps) left attention too soft for stochastic decoding on 7-14-line contexts even though greedy decoding and loss were unchanged: the emergent q/k-norm sharpness QK-norm removes is what the temperature-0.8 sampler needs, not a brittle artifact. Seed 2 had the lowest val loss (0.081) and the lowest metric (578), another case of pretrain loss not predicting the RL outcome. The ~27% step cost (fused LayerNorm + gain on q/k in an eager, launch-bound step) is a second, separable reason not to retry this at width 384 without torch.compile.",
